From 30f491271bddff07eef452fed539dfb6bf8f2272 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <david@katalystnord.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:59:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] ggml-cpu: flash attention LSE output and the
 grouped-query decode path from beast

Ported from the split attention series on beast (patches 0101, 0102, 0002 and
v2 0005, 0006, 0008):
- optional per-row log-sum-exp output of CPU flash attention
  (ggml_flash_attn_ext_set_lse, in the private header ggml/src/ggml-fa-lse.h so
  ggml.h and the CUDA objects do not change);
- grouped-query decode: each K/V row read once for all query heads sharing it,
  whole rows when the KV heads lie side by side in a row, blocks of 16 rows with
  the V accumulators in registers, q8_0 K scores in batches and the softmax exp
  8 rows at a time (AVX2).

fa-cpu (one query, 16 heads over 4 KV heads of 256, q8_0 K, q4_0 V, 16K tokens,
i7-9750H, 6 threads): 8.9 -> 13.0 GB/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
